{
  "about": "Evaluation set for 'Ask your own question' (SPEC Prompt-a-path, D-077). Each case: the prompt, the slice the user is in (scope), what code should end up showing (expect; arrays mean any of these), and a faked AI reply (fake) for the unit tests. fakeOnly cases use a deliberately wrong AI reply to prove code catches it; npm run eval:ask skips them, since a real model shouldn't produce them. Specs: fields in any order, aggregate defaults to sum, filters in any order.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "build-plain",
      "prompt": "Which genre brings in the most revenue?",
      "expect": { "outcome": "build", "spec": { "fields": ["genre", "revenue"], "aggregate": "sum", "filters": [] } },
      "fake": { "outcome": "build", "category": "none", "spec": { "fields": ["genre", "revenue"], "aggregate": "sum", "filters": [] }, "candidates": [], "term": "" }
    },
    {
      "id": "build-typo",
      "prompt": "revenu by genere",
